  <slave-step-copy-partition-distribution>
  </slave-step-copy-partition-distribution>
  <slave_workflow>N</slave_workflow>
  <groups>
  </groups>
  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>About: AePS 4-way reconciliation. NPCI settlement master (driving side) is LEFT-joined on RRN to the UIDAI
Aadhaar auth gateway, the BC micro-ATM terminal journal and the BC agent float GL-9904.
STP rule: STATUS=SUCCESS and AUTH_STATUS=SUCCESS and DISPENSE_STATUS=DISPENSED and GL_STATUS=POSTED and zero GL variance.
Exceptions: TERMINAL_TIMEOUT_91 / _96, DISPENSE_FAILURE, BIOMETRIC_MISMATCH, BIOMETRIC_SPOOF_ALERT (UIDAI 998),
GL_FLOAT_VARIANCE, GL_NOT_POSTED, BC_AGENT_MISMATCH, MISSING_IN_UIDAI / TERMINAL / GL, STATUS_MISMATCH.
Txn date / age is decoded from the RRN (YDDDHHnnnnnn) for the RBI T+1 TAT check downstream.

Params: INPUT_DIR, OUTPUT_DIR (config), CYCLE_ID (runtime).
Output: Matched_AePS_Records_&lt;yyyyMMdd_HHmmss&gt;.xlsx and Unmatched_AePS_Records_&lt;yyyyMMdd_HHmmss&gt;.xlsx; both paths are
returned as o_matched_file / o_unmatched_file and attached to the workflow result.

Errors: feeds are pre-validated (exists and non-empty) - a missing feed ends in Failure with the feed names.
Malformed CSV rows go down per-feed error hops to the error log (their RRN surfaces as a MISSING_IN_x exception).</note>
